d the Mauritian sense of place without legible brands: Chinatown gate in s06_chinatown_gate, Caudan canal with Le Pouce in s07_waterfront_pouce, Champ de Mars and Le Pouce in s09_see_mountains, and the harbour cranes in s13_crate_harbour.", "The 'own image everywhere' irony is delivered wordlessly in s08_own_image, where the living dodo confronts its mural and souvenir likenesses — the thematic heart of the search section.", "The capture added in s12b_crate_closed pays off: hands closing the slatted lid in front of the phone-holding crowd makes the transition from surrounded s11_surrounded to taken s13_crate_harbour causally clear.", "The ending is genuinely affecting: the walk in s18_walk_to_mural, the head pressed to the peeling painted forest in s19_press_mural and the mirrored sleep in s21_sleep_again earn the end card in s22_end_card."], "weaknesses": ["Continuity of scale and space slips at the climax of the attraction section: the intimate crowd of s11_surrounded becomes a vast overhead throng in s12_crowd_wide, and the crate then shrinks in s14_park_arrival, undercutting the otherwise careful realism.", "The reveal in s15_many_behind_glass is visually striking but narratively muddy — five similar dodos behind glass, with no clear sign the protagonist has joined them until the reverse angle in s16_phones_flashes.", "Human rendering is the main visual-quality risk: in s11_surrounded and s16_phones_flashes hands multiply around phones and blurred faces smear, sitting uneasily with the brief's 'no close-ups of faces' restraint.", "The mural climax is slightly under-animated: in s19_press_mural the dodo mostly lowers its head beside the wall rather than clearly pressing its body against the painted forest as the story intends.", "Emotional pacing flattens between s15_many_behind_glass and s18_walk_to_mural, where three similar enclosure setups in a row delay the mural payoff."]}
